# UI Components

Every visible control in this project is a shadcn/ui component from
`components/ui/`. Do not create custom UI. Do not hand-roll a button, link
styled as a button, input, textarea, select, checkbox, dialog, card, menu,
dropdown, or any other control. Do not add another component library, and do
not restyle a native element into a control. If a control is missing, add it
from the shadcn registry and use that generated component. The only extras
allowed on top of those components are layout (flex, gap, alignment) and the
theme tokens below.

shadcn is already initialized. [components.json](mdc:components.json) is the source
of truth for the configuration: the style is `radix-nova` (Radix UI primitives, Nova
preset), with CSS variables, the `neutral` base color, and `lucide` icons. Theme
tokens live in [app/globals.css](mdc:app/globals.css). Generated components go in
`components/ui/` and are owned by this repo, so they can be edited directly.

## Clerk sign-in and sign-up

Sign-in and sign-up are launched only from shadcn `Button` components. Wrap
each button in Clerk's `SignInButton` or `SignUpButton` with `mode="modal"`,
so Clerk opens its sign-in or sign-up flow in a modal on the current page.
Do not pass `asChild`: this project's `@clerk/nextjs` clones the child and
forwards leftover props onto it, so `asChild` leaks onto the shadcn `Button`.
Do not use Clerk's default button, a plain `<button>`, a styled link, or a
mounted `<SignIn />` / `<SignUp />` component as the control that starts auth.

```tsx
import { SignInButton, SignUpButton } from "@clerk/nextjs"
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"

<SignInButton mode="modal">
  <Button variant="outline">Sign in</Button>
</SignInButton>
<SignUpButton mode="modal">
  <Button>Sign up</Button>
</SignUpButton>
```

## Adding a component

`npx` fails in this environment with "Access is denied" because npm binary shims are
blocked, which is also why the scripts in [package.json](mdc:package.json) invoke
`node node_modules/...` directly. Use the `ui` script instead, which runs the locally
installed shadcn CLI:

```bash
npm run ui -- add button
```

Several components can be added in one call: `npm run ui -- add dialog input label`.
Add `--yes` to skip prompts in a non-interactive shell.

If shadcn is ever not initialized (no `components.json`), re-run init with the same
base and preset so generated components stay consistent:

```bash
npm install -D shadcn
npm run ui -- init --base radix --preset nova --yes
```

The canonical upstream commands are `npx shadcn@latest init` and
`npx shadcn@latest add button`; they are equivalent but will not run here.

## Conventions

CLI v4 components import the class helper from the `cn` package rather than from
`@/lib/utils`:

```tsx
import { cn } from "cn"
```

[lib/utils.ts](mdc:lib/utils.ts) re-exports `cn` and exists only for compatibility
with older shadcn examples. Match whichever import the surrounding file already uses.

Style components with the theme tokens (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`,
`border-border`, and so on) rather than raw Tailwind palette colors like `bg-zinc-50`,
so light and dark mode both stay correct. This project is in dark mode so make sure there are no dark colored text on dark backgrounds and vice versa.
